- **Kiln:** The masonry body reads as grounded and continuous, with a coherent tapered chimney and intentional open flue. The service canopy has a continuous roof surface, supported posts and visible footings. Its working area remains accessible from the open sides. The hearth close-up shows a recessed, brick-lined chamber with a floor and grate; the fire sits inside that chamber. The concentric front rings are visually unusual but do not establish a structural defect. The hanging sign has visible chains and projecting support brackets.

